MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_001: Ugh, crap, this wound hurts. Welp, better eat\nsomething first.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_002: Nezha? You're absolutely soaked! And how'd you get\nthat injury?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_003: Eh, ran into some trouble earlier. They made fun of\nme. Said I was a weird-looking punk.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_004: What have you done? If you were caught, the temple\nguards'd be locking you up right now.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_005: Hehe, well that'd work out nicely. Could give those\ntemple jerks a piece of my mind!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_006: That does it. We're out of options. Come here.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_007: Hey, where are you taking me? You're gonna turn me\nin to the temples, aren't you...
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_008: You're going to catch cold like that. And you need to\ndress that wound.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_009: Knock it off... My head's dry, my clothes are dry.\nI'm fine.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_010: Come on. Gimme your left arm. You need a proper\nbandaging.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_011: Gah, enough! Everyone treats me like I'm a kid!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_012: What is your problem?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_013: Sha Lan and Anatolia treat me like their baby\nbrother. Even Halvin started treating me that way...
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_014: She was acting like an older sister and fussing over\nme. I'm sick of being treated like a toddler!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_015: I mean, Anatolia and I were basically supposed to\nbe twins.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_016: So, how old are the two of you?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_017: How old? Um... Well, we were born in...1447, I think.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_018: Haha! Oh, come on. Stop making me laugh. You\nmust be at least 15.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_019: Wait, no, hang on. I'm older than that! I'm probably\nabout 17 or something. Yeah!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_020: Yeah, right. Either way, I've got you by a few years.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_021: Then...then I'm older than 17!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_022: Uh-huh. You know, getting all worked up about this\nkinda makes you still a kid.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_023: I get how you feel. But this is a time to simply say,\n"Thank you." That's the grown-up thing to do.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_024: Ugh, fiiine. Thank you.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_025: Awww, good boy!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_C_026: Damn it, so frustrating. I'm not gonna let this happen\never again.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_001: *sigh*
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_002: Hey, Ultand, you OK? Do you need some water?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_003: Thanks. I was just taking a little break.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_004: I was thinking about what lies ahead. The future is \nso unclear.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_005: What's up? Just a lot of smashing our enemies, right?\nSo what's the problem?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_006: Ever since Dagda made his announcement, the\ntemples have been in chaos.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_007: Some want to support the empire, and some don't.\nSome are on the fence. It's the same with the gods.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_008: Mars supports the kingdom of Brezarant. A war\nbetween gods is the last thing we need.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_009: I'm glad my family escaped, but I don't know what'll\nhappen to them...or to Aurora.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_010: I can't just sit here and fret all the time though. If I\nwant to protect everyone...now's the time to fight.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_011: Hey, don't be so hard on yourself. You tend to do that\na lot, don't you?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_012: Anyhow, I'm more suited for battle than you. If it\ncomes to it, I'll protect you.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_013: And here I was thinking you hated me.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_014: You once said you'd like to give temple folks a piece\nof your mind. What changed?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_015: I mean, they still annoy me. But I never felt that way\nabout you, even way back when.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_016: Probably because you remind me a bit of Sha Lan\nand Anatolia...
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_017: You know those two—the ones I grew up with.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_018: Hm. Is that an apology?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_019: You got so angry at me back then! You told me I was\nacting like your older sister.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_020: Well, yeah. I don't like being treated like a kid. I've\nhad plenty of that.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_021: Anyway, leave it to me! I'll tear through the enemies,\nand you can just kick back and relax!
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_022: Nezha, am I wrong, or did you grow up a little?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_023: Huh? My growth stopped once I was done being\nmanufactured. What are you getting at?
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_024: M-manufactured? Even so, you seem older.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_025: Pfft, I told you I can't grow any more. No matter\nwhat I do, this is as big as I'll ever be.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_026: I'm talking about personal growth. As in, you're\nbecoming more of an adult.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_027: You think so? Well, a Mediator's form isn't really\nchild or adult, when it comes down to it.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_028: You've cheered me up, Nezha. But I don't want you\nbehaving recklessly.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_029: C'mon. Don't go treating me like a kid again.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_030: Listen. I'm talking to you as a friend, OK? Let's just\nget through this alive.
MID_SE_Hur_Naz_B_031: Yeah.